  "id": "COMPOUND:18046 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Caesalpiniaphenol B is implicated in the interaction with CX-1 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link established via its targeting of SCCH-26 and LAPC4, both of which are known to be targets of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide. This compound, in turn, is shown to target CX-1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of CX-1. The evidence is supported by a consistent score of 0.5023 across three paths, indicating a plausible and robust relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of cellular targets that ultimately influence CX-1, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and the shared involvement of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide across different cell lines suggests a broader biological relevance, though further investigation is needed to confirm the specific role of Caesalpiniaphenol B in this process.",
